      "target": "../sections/sec-front-matter.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Bull. Org. mond. Sante\nBull. Wld Hith Org.\nj\nPossibilites d'amelioration des vaccins anticholeriques\net methodes d'evaluation de leur efficacite\nLOUIS DELPY,1 Dr Vet.\nLes doutes qui planent sur la valeur protectrice des vaccins anticholriques proviennent\nde diffierences importantes dans l'activite' immunisante de lots apparemment identiques. Ces\ndifferences ontpour cause l'insuffisance des titrages, et des techniques de preparation basees\nsur une conception errone'e du mode d'action des vaccins tue's.\nL'aptitude des vaccins anticholeriques a crder l'immunite ne peut e'tre mesure'e que par\ndes",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The opening of a French Bulletin article by Louis Delpy on improving cholera vaccines and assessing their efficacy, whose abstract argues that uneven protection comes from poor titration and from preparation methods based on a wrong view of how killed vaccines work. It states that protection depends on the amount of bacterial lysis products, not on counts of fixed bacteria, and proposes vaccines made from stabilized autolysates. The text then reviews natural immunity after cholera, which rarely lasts beyond six months, and stresses that antibodies detectable in vitro do not necessarily indicate protection.",
        "state": "draft",
        "draftedBy": {
          "kind": "agent",
          "id": "claude-code",
          "model": "not-disclosed"
        },
        "draftedAt": "2026-11-11"
