    {
      "id": "library/10665-266751/blocks/prose-sec-009",
      "types": [
        "folio-assistant-core:Prose",
        "doco:Section"
      ],
      "kind": "prose",
      "title": "SUMMARY",
      "pageStart": 9,
      "pageEnd": 10,
      "target": "../sections/sec-009-summary.md",
      "narrative": null,
      "content": "Over 60 years' experience have amply demonstrated the\nvalue of cholera vaccine\nin protecting man against\nnatural cholera infection, but statistical proof of its\nefficacy is still wanting.\nPublished statistics are often\ncriticized, but their deficiencies lie at least partly in the\ngeographic, climatic, administrative, medical and social\n1 Document de travail non publie, WHO/BS/IR/47.\nconditions that obtain at the time of cholera epidemics\nand that contribute to the persistence of cholera in certain\nareas. A vaccine may make it possible to put down an\nepidemic without its efficacy being statisti",
      "truncated": true,
      "provenance": "ingested",
      "summary": {
        "status": "draft",
        "text": "The English summary notes that cholera vaccine seems to protect but lacks statistical proof, and that differing expert views may reflect uneven vaccine potency. It explains that hidden autolysis makes vaccines of equal titre differ in immunogenicity and recommends stabilized autolysates with an adjuvant.",
        "state": "draft",
